Kelsey Finder: the beacon advertises as "Kelsey Finder", and nothing built carries Qorvo's name.

Qorvo's QANI advertises "<BoardName> (<DEVICEADDR[0] in hex>)", such as "DWM3001CDK (86E7C53A)". With this patch every
board built from it advertises "Kelsey Finder", and a phone tells boards apart by their Bluetooth identity. The
application's name, which the firmware logs, loses "Qorvo" too: Qorvo's licence (LicenseRef-QORVO-2, clause 5) lets
nothing built from its source carry Qorvo's name. Both files are LicenseRef-QORVO-2, and their notices are untouched.

Apply from the SDK source's root: patch -p1 < 0001-kelsey-finder-name.patch (qani/build does).

--- a/Projects/FreeRTOS/QANI/Common/src/main.c
+++ b/Projects/FreeRTOS/QANI/Common/src/main.c
@@ -94,7 +94,8 @@

     /* Start BLE */
     char advertising_name[32];
-    snprintf(advertising_name, sizeof(advertising_name), "%s (%08X)", (char *)BoardName, (unsigned int)NRF_FICR->DEVICEADDR[0]);
+    /* Kelsey Finder: the board name alone, so every beacon built here advertises as "Kelsey Finder". */
+    snprintf(advertising_name, sizeof(advertising_name), "%s", (char *)BoardName);
     ble_init(advertising_name);

     QLOGI("Application: %s", ApplicationName);
--- a/Projects/FreeRTOS/QANI/DWM3001CDK/ProjectDefinition/ProjectName.c
+++ b/Projects/FreeRTOS/QANI/DWM3001CDK/ProjectDefinition/ProjectName.c
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
  *
  */

-const char ProjectName[] = "DWM3001CDK - QANI - FreeRTOS";
-const char BoardName[] = "DWM3001CDK";
+const char ProjectName[] = "Kelsey Finder - DWM3001CDK - FreeRTOS";
+const char BoardName[] = "Kelsey Finder";
 const char OsName[] = "FreeRTOS";
-const char ApplicationName[] = "Qorvo Nearby Interaction";
+const char ApplicationName[] = "Kelsey Finder";
